1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Why was the first tunnel not completed?
第一条隧道为什么没有完工？

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,210
Why was the first tunnel not completed?
第一条隧道为什么没有完工？

3
00:00:16,230 --> 00:00:22,860
In 1858, a French engineer,
1858年，一位法国工程师

4
00:00:22,880 --> 00:00:26,930
Aime Thome de Gamond,
艾梅·托梅·德·加蒙

5
00:00:26,950 --> 00:00:33,630
arrived in England with a plan for a 21-mile tunnel under the English Channel.
带着一项在英吉利海峡下面开凿一条21英里长隧道的计划来到英国。

6
00:00:33,650 --> 00:00:40,570
He said that it would be possible to build a platform in the centre of the Channel.
他说可以在海峡中央建造一个平台。

7
00:00:40,590 --> 00:00:45,630
This platform would serve as a port and a railway station.
这个平台将用作港口和火车站。

8
00:00:45,650 --> 00:00:52,850
The tunnel would be well-ventilated if tall chimneys were built above sea level.
如果在海平面以上建起高高的烟囱，隧道的通风就会很好。

9
00:00:52,900 --> 00:00:59,790
In 1860, a better plan was put forward by an Englishman, William Low.
1860年，一位叫威廉·洛的英国人提出了一项更好的计划。

10
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:05,310
He suggested that a double railway-tunnel should be built.
他建议修建一条双轨铁路隧道。

11
00:01:05,330 --> 00:01:11,170
This would solve the problem of ventilation for if a train entered this tunnel,
这将解决通风问题，因为如果火车开进这条隧道，

12
00:01:11,190 --> 00:01:14,190
it would draw in fresh air behind it.
它会把新鲜空气抽进来跟在后面。

13
00:01:16,120 --> 00:01:19,810
Forty-two years later a tunnel was actually begun.
四十二年后，一条隧道真正开工了。

14
00:01:19,830 --> 00:01:24,700
If, at the time, the British had not feared invasion,
如果当时英国人不害怕入侵的话，

15
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:26,400
it would have been completed.
这条隧道早就建成了。

16
00:01:26,420 --> 00:01:33,210
The world had to wait almost another 100 years for the Channel Tunnel.
全世界为此又等了将近一百年才有了海峡隧道。

17
00:01:33,230 --> 00:01:38,010
It was officially opened on March 7, 1994,
它于1994年3月7日正式开通，

18
00:01:38,030 --> 00:01:41,910
finally connecting Britain to the European continent.
终于把英国和欧洲大陆连接了起来。
